     1	# eBPF Event Source
     2	
     3	Falco exposes BPF syscall events through a dedicated logical event source named
     4	`ebpf`. The source is backed by the same inspector and capture thread as the
     5	`syscall` source, so enabling it does not open another driver, allocate another
     6	buffer, or duplicate the event stream.
     7	
     8	## Event coverage
     9	
    10	The `ebpf` source accepts both BPF syscall event ABIs supported by
    11	falcosecurity/libs:
    12	
    13	- `PPME_SYSCALL_BPF_E` and `PPME_SYSCALL_BPF_X`
    14	- `PPME_SYSCALL_BPF_2_E` and `PPME_SYSCALL_BPF_2_X`
    15	
    16	All four event types have the Falco event name `bpf`. Rules can therefore use
    17	`evt.type=bpf` while selecting `source: ebpf`, and they will match modern eBPF
    18	drivers regardless of which ABI the driver emits.
